      "title": "Ukraine’s military says Starlink satellite connection stable after recent restrictions",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/ukraine-zelenskyy-military-starlink-satellite-connection-stable-after-restrictions",
      "description": "<p>But Elon Musk, whose company SpaceX owns Starlink, accuses Ukrainian military of violating ⁠the company’s terms</p><p>Ukraine’s military has a “stable connection to Starlink”, the Ukrainian government said, 10 days after its ability to use the satellite communications system <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/ukraine-soldiers-combat-access-starlink-satellite-internet-restricted\">was suddenly restricted</a>.</p><p>But hours after the announcement, SpaceX CEO Elon Musk, whose company owns Starlink, <a href=\"https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2114063986744275011\">accused</a> the Ukrainian military of violating ⁠the company’s terms. Neither Musk nor the US government, which operates Starshield using Starlink technology, took responsibility for imposing the curbs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/24/ukraine-zelenskyy-military-starlink-satellite-connection-stable-after-restrictions\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-24T21:25:58"
